WEBVTT

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:36.110
Top of the third inning.
Bijoudai Sayama High to bat.

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:36.820
Third batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Yano.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:37.740
Ready!

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.660
Third batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Yano.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:40.530
Play!

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:42.120
I won't swing if it's inside.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:43.580
If it's outside, it'll be a shootball.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:46.000
Inside.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:47.960
Strike!

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.290
It went in?

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:51.000
Well, those things happen, I guess.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:54.210
Strike!

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:56.380
Um...

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.550
Yano's favorite course.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.220
He won't swing, even if it's going in.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:04.520
Usually, after two throws to the inside, the next should go outside, right?

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.230
The only pitch he has left to escape to the outside with is his shootball.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:10.190
But I already hit it during my first at-bat.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:13.610
Maybe it'll be the fastball they talked about?

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:15.360
It's on the outside, but it's a curveball!

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.190
Strike!

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:18.150
Nice pitch!

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.370
They were swinging based on such thorough planning?

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.830
Now that we know, it's easy enough to deal with.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:27.620
We can't worry about the four runs we allowed in the first two innings.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.420
Fourth batter. Center fielder: Number 8, Wada.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:31.330
Ready!

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:33.670
All right, it's a power hitter.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:37.670
Wada likes the outside corner,
and he's already hit an inside slider.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:40.550
He's only hitting balls that aren't in his preferred course.

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:43.430
Outside. A shootball that curves out.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:46.890
Um... A ball to the outside course that Wada likes.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:49.520
He'll watch it pass and it'll be 0-1 again, won't it?

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:53.690
It's fine. As long as I throw as Abe says...

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.070
Ball!

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:58.280
The first pitch is the same as last time?

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.070
How about the second one?

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:02.620
Inside! The home run pitch!

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:03.280
Strike!

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.200
A shootball?

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:09.410
After that homer, I guess I won't be getting the same pitch.

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:11.250
But it felt like it went in.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:16.090
I wonder if they think the outside corner is still safe, even after that home run?

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:21.880
A slider to the inside is what he got a home run on before...

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:23.260
But it doesn't matter.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:27.470
If he gives me the sign to throw it, I'll throw it!

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:28.850
Inside! Swing!

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:33.270
Out!

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:34.520
Two outs!

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.980
Following Abe's lead is working out after all.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:37.780
Now then,

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:40.740
we finally know the opponent's strategy.
If they change it, we'll lose our advantage.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.820
Fifth batter. Right fielder: Number 9, Miyata.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:46.700
I want the other side to think that we haven't realized a thing yet.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:50.200
Ball!

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.370
A ball to my preferred outside course.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.080
It's all in line with the rule.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:57.420
The second is a curveball to the outside.

00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.420
It's so difficult.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:04.720
Even though I'm looking at the same data as Abe, I can't predict his lead at all.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:06.140
Ball!

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:07.560
Outside.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:10.470
The pitch type is off, but it was a ball to the outside as expected.

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.100
I figure he'll go for a strike next.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.730
If I'm right, it'll be inside.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:17.940
To get me focused on outside pitches with that curveball, he'll send a shootball at my chest.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:20.070
Opposite!

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.240
Out!

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:26.320
Roka.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:30.830
Looks like you're utilizing that info, huh?

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.870
Nice pitching.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.040
N-Nice lead.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.580
You didn't shake your head.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:37.670
Yeah.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:38.750
Did you want to?

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.130
No.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:43.670
I want to follow your lead.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:48.470
Because that's the best way.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:51.810
Doing what Abe says is best for me!

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.680
Hey, Tajima!

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:54.940
Do that thing from before.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:55.690
Just now?

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:58.230
What was it... that, uh, instant...

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:04.530
You're relaxed now, right?

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:07.200
It's fine to go for a clean hit. Get on base!

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.740
Yeah! Thanks!

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.950
Bottom of the third inning.
Nishiura High to bat.
All right! I'm going to hit it!

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:14.160
Just watch, Bijou. I'll get our first run!

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.830
Eighth batter. Left fielder: Number 7, Mizutani.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:19.380
All right, how are they shifting for me?

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.710
The outfielders...

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.260
They're pretty far forward.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:26.090
I guess I won't be able to scrape one past the infielders?

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:29.510
Try to imagine what kind of batter they think I am...

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:34.310
Um... Is there anything important other than my weak swing?

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:37.020
Just watch the first pitch.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.150
Ready!

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.440
Now I get it.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.730
If I don't see the pitch, I won't know.

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:44.900
We can take it easy this inning.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:48.660
We can hold them off like this until the fourth inning. Takumi still has another three at-bats...

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.200
and Ryuu's shoulder will hold out for the last two innings.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:54.660
Strike!

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:55.830
Swing!

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.370
Make it bounce, Mizutani! Close your armpits!

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.120
My armpits?

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.840
Whoa, it tickles!

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.840
Yeah!

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.260
One, two...

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:08.800
Nice batting!

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:10.340
That was awesome!

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:11.430
Nice batting!

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.810
Being ticklish revived me.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:18.730
For the first time, I think I understand what it means to close my armpits and hit the ball!

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:21.020
No outs with a runner on base.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:22.190
I have to tread carefully.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:25.230
They scored easily in the first two innings...

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.440
because they read through
the battery's mix of pitches.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:31.740
The battery's mix of pitches...
She means Abe's mix of pitches.

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.950
I'm absolutely useless.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:37.910
Abe always has trouble putting
things together with my pitches.

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:41.790
We can't afford to lose
because of those four points.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.750
Ninth batter. Pitcher: Number 1, Mihashi.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:44.590
A bunt.

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:45.250
Ninth batter. Pitcher: Number 1, Mihashi.

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:47.300
I won't fail!

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.170
Mihashi!

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:51.760
Fingers. Watch your fingers.

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:53.680
W-What?

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.430
Fingers! Your fingers!

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:59.600
It's impossible. Impossible?

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:00.890
Th-The bunt!?

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:04.860
I-It's not impossible. I can bunt.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:07.320
I told him not to hold it like that!

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:09.360
How noisy.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:11.860
Even if you don't say anything, he'll be careful.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:14.160
Trust in Mihashi a little.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:18.500
It's irritating how much Abe considers Mihashi an idiot.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:19.790
Though he <i>is</i> pretty stupid.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:25.710
I-I-It's not impossible.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:27.550
We'll score more than four runs.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:31.180
I won't let Abe blame himself.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:34.350
All right, in front of the pitcher! We can nail the runners!

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:35.760
Second!

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:36.430
Second base?

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:38.180
Safe!

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:41.600
Th-Thank goodness.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.560
Is he an idiot!?

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:45.230
That was risky.

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:48.070
This isn't the place to cross such dangerous bridges!

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:50.150
Now they're both safe.

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:54.110
I thought Miyata's response was appropriate, though.

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:56.450
The right fielder, Miyata.

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:59.410
He was the catcher when you played us, remember?

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.040
Shit.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:04.580
If my fielder's choice is this bad, I won't be able to face Miyata!

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:05.000
First batter. Center fielder: Number 8, Izumi.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.130
Don't rush it.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:09.380
According to the pattern, he won't give the order if there's a two-point difference.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:11.920
Good job, Mizutani and Mihashi!

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:14.220
I'll get you guys home.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:15.680
Bunt?

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:18.930
If this is the coach's assessment of me,

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:20.970
she must think I can keep my cool while being underestimated.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:23.190
Even if there are runners, he won't be bunting.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:25.440
The outfielder's positions are forward as expected.

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:30.860
Even though a bunt wouldn't be that odd right now, they're staying at midfield?

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:33.360
They don't think I'll bunt.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:34.700
I understand.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:36.320
I'll do a proper bunt.

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.240
Plus, the runners are Mizutani and Mihashi.

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:39.790
I'll definitely make it.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:42.410
First!

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:44.120
Out!

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:45.330
All right! Second and third!

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:46.170
Izumi.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:46.500
Second batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Sakaeguchi.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:48.040
H-He's good.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:50.090
Not a squeeze?

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:51.000
Second batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Sakaeguchi.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:56.260
Even if they're looking out for a squeeze,
we've never gone for the first pitch.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:58.550
There's a good chance that they'll put a strike in.

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:00.930
Aim for the first pitch?

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.720
I wonder what'll come...

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:03.520
Okay!

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:06.020
He hasn't thrown a shootball yet today!

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:08.730
The third runner... What's he smiling about?

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:10.480
A shoot!

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:11.860
Third!

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:12.730
It'll pass third!

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:14.570
Go!

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:17.570
First run!

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:25.290
First!

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:27.330
Out!

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:28.540
Fourth batter. Third baseman: Number 5, Tajima.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:29.380
Ready!

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:30.840
Here he comes!

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:31.710
Fourth batter. Third baseman: Number 5, Tajima.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:34.800
Out of all the Nishiura players, this guy's clearly the best.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.050
To end the winning streak of this bloodsucking team of first years,

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:40.050
holding him back is crucial.

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:42.640
You're our ace.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:45.310
Yoshito, I'm counting on you for
the sake of our other pitchers, too.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:48.060
Even though there's a runner, he's doing a big windup.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:52.520
Strike!

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:53.480
Okay.

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:54.990
A lot of heat behind this one.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:02.740
Strike!

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:03.990
Changeup.

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:05.040
All right.

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:07.960
Another fastball? Or will he go in for the kill?

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.550
A-Amazing.

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:16.800
It was a shootball.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:20.260
Up until now, the mix of pitches has been: fastball, changeup, shoot.

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:23.470
Adding in the fastball, this guy has four pitches.

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:25.060
The remaining pitch type is...

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:28.890
There!

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:30.770
Strike!

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:32.110
Yeah!

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:34.690
Nice pitching! That was the best course!

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:36.190
Takeshi, stop flattering me.

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:37.530
No, seriously.

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:40.570
Even the pros wouldn't swing at that pitch.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.240
We managed to hold them at one run.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:46.370
It's still okay, right?

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:48.830
What?

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:50.330
I'm sorry.

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:51.460
What was the mix of pitches?

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.960
Fastball, changeup, shootball, slider.

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:57.130
So you've seen all four pitch types, huh?

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.130
Yes, ma'am!

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:01.550
Why did you make Kurata the
official catcher instead of Miyata?
Top of the fourth inning.
Bijoudai Sayama High to bat.

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:03.180
Because Kurata's better than Miyata, right?

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:03.550
Sixth batter. Left fielder: Number 7, Kitamura.

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:06.640
Please define your interpretation of "better."

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:09.520
I'm interested in what you value in a catcher, Roka.

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:13.190
Again.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:14.940
They just can't hit it right now.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:18.490
Out!

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.070
Five people in a row.

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:22.110
Shut up.

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:25.660
Eighth batter. Catcher: Number 2, Kurata.

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:26.490
Again?
Eighth batter. Catcher: Number 2, Kurata.

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:28.870
Hey, Roka.

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:30.830
What kind of personality does Kurata have?

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.880
A normal one.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:37.460
Right now, for better or worse, we only have normal people.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:40.170
Then is he really attached to you or something?

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:41.010
What?

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:43.180
He's been looking your way for a while now.

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:49.060
Don't tell me that you're secretly giving out signs from the stands or something?

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:55.230
Don't be ridiculous!

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:57.730
Stop being a pest and beat it.

00:11:57.730 --> 00:12:00.690
A loser from the first round shouldn't pretend this is any of his business.

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:06.030
This is bad.

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:08.830
Another three outs in a row.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:09.450
Damn it!

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:21.800
I'm even more tempted to stick around
when you try to cover it up so unnaturally.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:25.970
Did we overdo it?

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:29.970
If we get another hit, they might come up with a new plan.

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:31.980
Hey.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:35.060
You've been pitching more today; are you all right?

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:39.480
I want to win today, so... I'm all right!

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:41.690
Now that I think about it, he's been saying that since morning.

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:44.070
Is there a special reason why he wants to win today?

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:47.160
If we win today, we'll enter the best eight.

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:51.450
Well, whatever. That's fine.

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:54.870
For that reason, you'd better watch out for injuries, too.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:57.330
When you're bunting, don't
hang over the plate too much.

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:59.170
Don't make me repeat that.

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:01.050
Pitcher is different from other positions.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:03.090
Deception won't work.

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:05.180
You need to understand that already.

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:07.680
I see.

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:09.510
I shouldn't have hung over the plate.

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:16.480
I averted my eyes! What the hell am I
supposed to do after averting my eyes like that?

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:17.980
Come on, say it one more time!

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:19.650
Hey!

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:22.070
I'm going to score some runs this inning!

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:24.240
Your hands...

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:29.370
I-I... want to win today.

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:32.660
I-If Hanai scores a run, we'll be able to win!

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:35.370
Hanai.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:38.080
Pull the ball.

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:40.960
Show them what you can do.

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:45.380
Bottom of the fourth inning.
Nishiura High to bat.

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:47.300
Come on! Hit it!

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:50.180
Yeah!
Fifth batter. Right fielder: Number 9, Hanai.

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:52.810
Just as the second baseman and shortstop are leaning towards the inside,

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:54.720
the third baseman is too.

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:57.390
During middle school, I hit it past the third's flank a lot.

00:13:57.390 --> 00:13:59.350
I'll aim towards there.

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:02.400
Strike!

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:04.820
It came in fast.

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:07.570
Nice pitch!

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:09.700
All right. This swing seals it.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:13.990
Damn, this is fun.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:18.160
Fair!

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:20.130
Third!

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:27.840
That felt good!

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:29.970
Although he'd normally pull the ball,

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:32.100
to be able to pull off such a sharp hit...

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:32.470
Sixth batter. First Baseman: Number 3, Oki.

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:34.220
Not to mention Mizutani's play in the third inning!

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:36.810
High schoolers really improve by leaps and bounds!

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:38.270
Now then, Oki. Keep firm and steady!

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:39.190
Ready!

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:39.980
Now then, Oki. Keep firm and steady!

00:14:44.770 --> 00:14:47.320
Even though I'm the sixth batter, I've barely hit at all.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.070
I at least have to bunt properly.

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:50.990
Even Mihashi managed to do it.

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:52.120
Don't get scared!

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:55.330
Out!

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:57.410
Nice bunt!

00:14:57.410 --> 00:15:00.620
Crap! They might come around to me!

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:02.420
Izumi!

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:05.130
Seventh batter. Catcher: Number 2, Abe.

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.630
Can you do "that"?

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:07.510
Okay!

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:13.720
Ball!

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:17.060
Why did you start with a ball!? Idiot!

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.100
There's no squeeze? Really?

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:20.230
Shit.

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:21.850
The coach's orders are absolute.

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:24.230
If I stumble, the team will get rattled.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:29.940
Strike!

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:32.160
Batter, take it easy! Third runner!

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:34.030
Oh yeah, third runner.

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.040
The second pitcher is heading out.

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:39.200
So Takenouchi's done after this inning?

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:40.660
No wonder he's working it so hard.

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:45.130
He seemed tricky, but it doesn't
look like there'll be a squeeze here.

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:47.670
The seventh batter thinks he can hit my pitch, huh?

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:51.970
Sorry, but your female
coach's predictions are off!

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:53.510
Strike!

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:55.180
Nice pitch...

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:56.180
Mizutani hit it already!

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:57.640
Eighth batter. Left fielder: Number 7, Mizutani.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:15:59.140
It's time to get fired up!

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:02.600
I'm "Nice Batting" Mizutani today!
Eighth batter. Left fielder: Number 7, Mizutani.

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:04.190
Strike!

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:07.820
Coach Momo is glaring at me.
Watch closely!

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:08.940
Watch carefully. Watch carefully.

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:09.860
Go for it!

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:11.820
Watch carefully.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:15.070
He hit it!

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:17.580
Second run!

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:19.950
Told you I'd score one!

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:22.580
High five, high five!

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:23.670
Do it normally!

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:31.090
Shit.

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:34.340
What is this embarrassing feeling like I've just been forced to play house?

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:37.300
When we score runs, do a high five.

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:38.680
Mizutani's pretty good!

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:39.720
Is it because he was tickled?

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:40.060
Ninth batter. Pitcher: Number 1, Mihashi.

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:41.020
What should we do?

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:42.850
Should we start tickling everyone?

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:43.690
Ninth batter. Pitcher: Number 1, Mihashi.

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:45.850
If that'll get us hits, then let's do it!

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:48.440
What should we do about
the guys who aren't ticklish?

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:51.400
Well, I mean, my armpits aren't ticklish.

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:52.280
Same here.

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:54.240
That's so weird!

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:55.660
It's not weird.

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:56.990
It's normal.

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:58.030
What's wrong?

00:16:58.030 --> 00:16:59.910
Mihashi, close your armpits!

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:00.580
Armpits!?

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:02.700
Strike!

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:07.210
We managed to make up another run.

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:10.840
Even if I can't hit it, the others will score.

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:13.090
Fifth inning! Let's shut them down!

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:15.550
Yeah!

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:18.510
This is a team.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:21.100
Ready!
Ninth batter. Pitcher: Number 1, Takenouchi.

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.560
It looks like they know our strategy,

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:25.940
but with this guy's pitches, I should be able to hit it.

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:28.060
The pattern's been changed, so a slider to the inside...

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:29.770
A ball? No, it's in!

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:31.820
First batter. Shortstop: Number 6, Kawashima.

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:33.900
With no outs and one runner on base, we're back on top!

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:35.860
Ready!
First batter. Shortstop: Number 6, Kawashima.

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:38.820
We ended up letting a
runner on base with no outs.

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:41.780
Takenouchi swung at his favored course,

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:45.790
so I think they know that I'm
using their strategy against them.

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:48.620
But that just means we're on equal footing!

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:49.880
Ball!

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.750
He started with a ball.

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:53.380
I still can't believe it,

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:56.130
but with this pitcher,
it's not due to loss of control.

00:17:58.340 --> 00:17:59.010
Ball!

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:00.970
He's doing it on purpose.

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:03.350
Two balls means they're trying to lure me out.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:04.390
According to the data,

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:08.020
with no strikes and two balls, a breaking ball
that changes from a strike to a ball came next.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:11.480
In other words, if it's outside, it's a slider.
If it's inside, it's a shootball.

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:13.650
No matter how much you try to hide it,

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:18.570
as long as you're using this pitcher, your mind is like an open book!

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:21.740
Second!

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:24.540
No outs with runners on first and third base!

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:26.040
No outs!

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:28.120
Watch for infield hits and
keep an eye on home plate!

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:29.830
First and third base! Watch out for a squeeze!

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:34.590
Two hits in a row!?
Are we really on equal ground?

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:37.220
I don't want to let them score any more runs.

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:37.800
Second batter. Third baseman: Number 5, Ishikawa.
I don't want to let them score any more runs.

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:41.930
The only thing I can do is follow Abe's lead.
Second batter. Third baseman: Number 5, Ishikawa.

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:47.140
Strike!

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:47.930
All right!

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:49.730
It went in!?

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:52.650
In this situation, there's no way
they're not prepared for a squeeze,

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:55.650
but it also means that we can't
shake that pitcher with just a stance.

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:58.570
We managed to get 0-1, so we've got a little more breathing room.

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:01.950
I want to send the second pitch wide while still watching for a squeeze.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:04.910
But if we make it 0-2, it'll be ours.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:07.290
Don't be scared!

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:10.120
A fast one... Fastball!

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:11.540
Strike!

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:14.710
I can make it!

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:15.920
Runner on first ran!

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:18.510
It's in! I can't let it fly!

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:21.300
First!

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:22.720
Out!

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:24.550
All right! Well done!

00:19:25.300 --> 00:19:27.260
Yano! Bring us home!

00:19:27.260 --> 00:19:29.230
Third batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Yano.

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:32.190
There's only one out. Hit it to the
outfield and we've got another run!

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:33.980
Concentrate on the batter.

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:36.150
If you relax your guard,
two of them will return home!

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:39.240
He's hit the shootball. We've also
shown him the curveball and the slider.

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:41.700
It doesn't matter what comes.

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:43.780
If he gets it to the outfield, that's one more run!

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:45.660
We can't hold him back with a fastball.

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:48.870
If you give me the sign,
I'll throw whatever you want.

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:52.000
To finish him off with a dropping pitch, we'll need to throw a ball first.

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.840
As long as the hit's good, I'll head for home.

00:19:57.840 --> 00:20:00.170
We'll make up for that last run you scored!

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:02.590
Fastball!

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:04.300
A fastball?

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:05.550
He hit it up!

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:08.390
Go!

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:12.270
Fifth run!

00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:20.530
In the fertile green fields, the light shines...

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:21.240
Mihashi!

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:34.250
Even though I don't want
Abe to think it's his fault...

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:37.330
Even though we finally got a run in...

00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:38.540
Mihashi.

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:40.880
You...

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:44.220
Can you still believe in my lead and pitch?

00:20:45.130 --> 00:20:46.720
I can!

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:49.350
I... can pitch!

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:53.890
I'm such an idiot!

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:56.560
What are you doing,
pushing your anxiety onto Mihashi!?

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:58.400
Get your act together!

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:01.320
I should be able to make
better use of his abilities!

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:02.570
Okay!

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:04.700
I'm counting on you for your best pitches!

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:05.530
Yeah!

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:07.200
Now then, let's keep it going in one shot.

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:10.490
Fourth batter. Center fielder: Number 8, Wada.

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:13.870
This guy's control should
really be an amazing weapon.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:16.790
But when their mix of pitches is seen through, it becomes a weak point.

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:20.000
The first pitch was a ball.

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:23.760
They must think that a ball is necessary when facing me.

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:25.970
In order to see what ball I'm aiming for...

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:27.800
Did he just shake his head?

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:30.300
Which means it's not a ball!

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:32.260
Strike!

00:21:32.260 --> 00:21:33.680
He caught my attention.

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:36.390
This time, he hasn't shaken his head.

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:40.230
Strike!

00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:44.190
It's to the outside again! Did I just swing at two balls in a row?

00:21:45.650 --> 00:21:46.950
Again!

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:48.910
Don't get confused by a simple headshake!

00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:51.120
It'd be weirder if he didn't shake his head.

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:54.370
Shoot? No!

00:21:54.370 --> 00:21:55.250
Strike!

00:21:56.120 --> 00:21:57.620
I didn't give up a hit!

00:21:57.620 --> 00:21:58.540
Nice pitch!

00:21:58.540 --> 00:22:00.330
Just now... That was his quirky ball?

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:03.130
He swung on all three balls.

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:06.800
I can't tell if he was confused by Mihashi shaking his head or not!

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:09.970
Abe's lead is amazing!

00:23:41.690 --> 00:23:46.900
With Mizutani contributing as well, Nishiura has caught up to a three-point difference.

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:51.360
Mihashi and Abe's battery is also back in good shape again.

00:23:51.360 --> 00:23:53.950
From now on, it's Nishiura's counterattack.

00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:59.580
Bijoudai Sayama's second pitcher,
Kashima, is finally making his appearance.

00:24:00.080 --> 00:24:04.830
Will Nishiura be able to capture Kashima's quick pitches?

00:24:04.830 --> 00:24:05.500
Next time:

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:08.130
Bottom of the 5th Inning, 2 to 5.

00:24:08.130 --> 00:24:09.840
Do a big high five!
